I'm happy he's growing.

101
00:20:41,260 --> 00:20:46,510
As he grows, we grow too.

102
00:20:47,580 --> 00:20:51,170
Who will we support if we don't
support Osman Bey?

103
00:20:52,000 --> 00:20:55,730
Whatever you give to Osman Bey, you'll
take back the double.

104
00:20:56,570 --> 00:20:58,520
We always supported him.

105
00:21:01,290 --> 00:21:03,830
Inshallah...

106
00:21:05,100 --> 00:21:06,640
we get what we deserve.

107
00:21:08,870 --> 00:21:10,090
You will.

108
00:21:10,190 --> 00:21:12,860
As long as we support Osman Bey...

109
00:21:13,940 --> 00:21:16,340
it's his fault if we don't
gain anything.

110
00:21:16,990 --> 00:21:17,990
You're right.

111
00:21:18,270 --> 00:21:19,270
Come on.

112
00:21:28,470 --> 00:21:31,760
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim. (in the name of
Allah, the merciful and compassionate.)

113
00:21:44,770 --> 00:21:48,730
Even İnegöl is ours now.

114
00:21:49,750 --> 00:21:52,430
We have the fruits of our labor, huh?

115
00:21:52,840 --> 00:21:54,220
Yes but...

116
00:21:54,720 --> 00:21:58,080
I'm afraid if we pluck them too early.

117
00:21:58,190 --> 00:22:00,010
What fruits, Beys?

118
00:22:02,230 --> 00:22:03,570
The fruits are plucked.

119
00:22:04,340 --> 00:22:07,180
Trees are billets, billets are ships now.

120
00:22:07,550 --> 00:22:10,030
We are against the heathens in waves.

121
00:22:10,360 --> 00:22:12,840
As Osman Bey is here...

122
00:22:13,290 --> 00:22:14,980
don't worry.

123
00:22:23,550 --> 00:22:26,070
May the peace of Allah be upon you.

124
00:22:26,630 --> 00:22:28,870
May the peace of Allah be upon you.

125
00:22:37,030 --> 00:22:39,170
O, the owner of everything.

126
00:22:41,330 --> 00:22:42,330
My Allah.

127
00:22:45,360 --> 00:22:48,040
Everything you grant us comes from you.

128
00:22:49,980 --> 00:22:51,340
It's yours.

129
00:22:52,730 --> 00:22:53,490
My Allah...

130
00:22:54,490 --> 00:22:56,720
I want to rule these lands
that you gave me...

131
00:22:58,120 --> 00:23:01,770
properly.

132
00:23:03,970 --> 00:23:06,190
Don't disappoint me.

133
00:23:08,270 --> 00:23:09,270
My Allah...

134
00:23:11,050 --> 00:23:17,750
let me rule these lands ethically.

135
00:23:18,980 --> 00:23:26,690
Grant us the dare to look at our Prophet
on the day of judgment (doomsday).

136
00:23:28,950 --> 00:23:29,950
Amin.

137
00:23:32,340 --> 00:23:33,340
Amin.

138
00:23:55,020 --> 00:23:58,140
Osman Bey!

139
00:24:13,260 --> 00:24:15,950
- Salam Alaikum.
- Alaikum Salam.

140
00:24:24,230 --> 00:24:25,890
Sit down.

141
00:24:31,920 --> 00:24:37,230
From now on, the meetings for
urgent problems are history.

142
00:24:39,140 --> 00:24:43,880
The era is new. The regulations are new.

143
00:24:47,400 --> 00:24:52,660
In the names of Allah's 99 names...

144
00:24:53,030 --> 00:24:56,410
who hold us responsible for our
victories...

145
00:24:58,840 --> 00:25:00,390
I'm opening the council.

146
00:25:00,550 --> 00:25:04,680
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim. (in the name of
Allah, the merciful and compassionate.)

147
00:25:05,100 --> 00:25:06,700
Tell me what's happening.

148
00:25:06,770 --> 00:25:09,960
The migrants are coming.

149
00:25:10,410 --> 00:25:15,280
As they keep coming like this, we won't
have enough weapons during the war.

150
00:25:15,860 --> 00:25:19,640
Mashallah.
They will come with their plentifulness.

151
00:25:20,210 --> 00:25:22,870
Blacksmiths are at their place.

152
00:25:23,410 --> 00:25:24,870
Bayındır Bey...

153
00:25:26,090 --> 00:25:28,010
tell me what is happening.

154
00:25:29,360 --> 00:25:33,010
We have lots of swords, thank Allah.

155
00:25:35,160 --> 00:25:37,520
What about Karaağaç place?

156
00:25:37,970 --> 00:25:40,580
Tell me.

157
00:25:43,300 --> 00:25:45,420
It's good, my Bey.

158
00:25:45,750 --> 00:25:48,970
People eat what they sow.

159
00:25:49,440 --> 00:25:52,980
Karaağaç is important.

160
00:25:53,730 --> 00:25:55,900
It's neighbors with the heathens' place.

161
00:25:56,710 --> 00:26:00,920
It's in barren lands, unlike Marmaracık.

162
00:26:02,810 --> 00:26:05,170
Why Marmaracık matters, my Bey?

163
00:26:05,320 --> 00:26:07,940
It's the door.

164
00:26:08,460 --> 00:26:11,090
A leg of Constantinople limps.

165
00:26:12,350 --> 00:26:17,070
We'll start to conquer before them.

166
00:26:18,170 --> 00:26:21,110
Constantinople
Emperor Palace

167
00:26:22,890 --> 00:26:25,900
Osman doesn't stop.
Won't stop.

168
00:26:26,300 --> 00:26:28,700
He may be getting
ready for a war now.

169
00:26:29,150 --> 00:26:31,930
We have to move before him.

170
00:26:32,300 --> 00:26:36,500
We can't. I'll deal with Osman
for now, Kantakuzenos.

171
00:26:36,660 --> 00:26:39,490
You can't rule Rome with fear.

172
00:26:40,230 --> 00:26:42,500
The Papacy is ready to help us.

173
00:26:42,620 --> 00:26:46,550
We can build a Crusader army and fight
our enemies if we want

174
00:26:47,060 --> 00:26:49,900
Only fools forget what happened.

175
00:26:50,350 --> 00:26:54,000
Do you expect me to trust those Catholics?
They are like our enemies.

176
00:26:55,220 --> 00:27:00,510
Be brave, Emperor. Will
you deal with Turks?

177
00:27:00,810 --> 00:27:03,130
They will come if we don't go.

178
00:27:03,230 --> 00:27:04,400
Enough!

179
00:27:05,390 --> 00:27:09,210
How dare you question Emperor's courage?
How dare you, Kantakuzenos!

180
00:27:10,770 --> 00:27:15,730
If I fight with the ones in hell, I won't
carry it to heaven.

181
00:27:16,340 --> 00:27:18,960
I want to destroy them.

182
00:27:19,490 --> 00:27:21,390
I always support you.

183
00:27:21,750 --> 00:27:23,360
If you excuse me.

184
00:27:27,240 --> 00:27:30,770
I support you.... because...

185
00:27:33,170 --> 00:27:39,220
If they see that we lose our ability, they
will attack us.

186
00:27:39,830 --> 00:27:45,260
That's why we will put up
walls out of stones.

187
00:27:46,290 --> 00:27:50,020
The duties you'll have...

188
00:27:51,380 --> 00:27:53,910
will be those walls' stones.

189
00:27:59,840 --> 00:28:01,510
Orhan Bey...

190
00:28:03,990 --> 00:28:07,320
it's time to experience your knowledge.

191
00:28:08,810 --> 00:28:12,600
Karacahisar Castle is under your rule now.

192
00:28:13,700 --> 00:28:15,870
Let us see what you do.

193
00:28:16,480 --> 00:28:18,280
Your command, my Bey.

194
00:28:23,840 --> 00:28:25,400
Alaaddin Bey.

195
00:28:27,630 --> 00:28:31,240
Continue your education.

196
00:28:35,000 --> 00:28:37,540
Your command, my Bey.

197
00:28:47,600 --> 00:28:50,660
You're the commander
of Yenişehir, Aktemur.

198
00:28:51,670 --> 00:28:53,480
Your word is my word, my Bey.

199
00:28:53,700 --> 00:28:56,120
You have so many responsibilities.

200
00:28:59,110 --> 00:29:00,310
Beys.

201
00:29:01,400 --> 00:29:04,390
We'll build a new bazaar in Yenişehir.

202
00:29:05,070 --> 00:29:07,080
Merchants will come.

203
00:29:08,050 --> 00:29:11,570
Even people will come offshore.

204
00:29:11,950 --> 00:29:16,030
That's why
we will have so many responsibilities.

205
00:29:16,450 --> 00:29:18,820
Turks need trade, my Bey.

206
00:29:19,390 --> 00:29:21,260
You can have our goods.

207
00:29:35,590 --> 00:29:37,940
The golds we earned from the war.

208
00:29:39,300 --> 00:29:44,530
This is a council, not a public purse.

209
00:29:45,390 --> 00:29:47,470
Give those to the poor people.

210
00:29:52,400 --> 00:29:56,320
There's no one in need in our lands.
Everyone is good thanks to you.

211
00:29:56,840 --> 00:30:00,130
I gave those to people in need.
This is what is left.

212
00:30:07,700 --> 00:30:10,970
Then, give those to Karaağaç people.

213
00:30:12,110 --> 00:30:14,430
He said they are in need.

214
00:30:15,790 --> 00:30:17,500
Thanks, my Bey.

215
00:30:21,580 --> 00:30:27,420
A Bey's word is a
command, tell us what to do!

216
00:30:33,510 --> 00:30:37,200
Mongols in the east, Rome in the west.

217
00:30:37,950 --> 00:30:40,490
They are attacking us from both sides.

218
00:30:40,790 --> 00:30:45,590
If we don't stand still upright...

219
00:30:47,890 --> 00:30:50,600
then we will be trapped under the debris.

220
00:30:51,570 --> 00:30:56,800
We're not afraid.

221
00:30:57,550 --> 00:31:03,260
This is such a big plane tree
that it grows every day.

222
00:31:03,990 --> 00:31:06,480
Oppressed people will
rest under its shadow.

223
00:31:07,170 --> 00:31:09,940
Of course, people will try to harm it.

224
00:31:11,660 --> 00:31:16,930
If we don't unite under its shadow
and don't attack the enemy...

225
00:31:17,330 --> 00:31:22,740
then, cruel people's shadow will be
over us.

226
00:31:24,930 --> 00:31:27,630
Beys are working.

227
00:31:27,850 --> 00:31:31,040
The fights for the throne still continue.

228
00:31:32,100 --> 00:31:34,830
We are with the oppressed people.

229
00:31:36,190 --> 00:31:42,060
We know we're alone but loneliness will
hold us together.

230
00:31:43,030 --> 00:31:46,670
It will give us strength.

231
00:31:48,750 --> 00:31:54,260
We live for this dream and move.

232
00:31:55,610 --> 00:32:00,950
We bring justice, we can't stop.

233
00:32:02,050 --> 00:32:03,440
Beys...

234
00:32:05,470 --> 00:32:10,540
if we stop, then we'll stay behind.

235
00:32:12,130 --> 00:32:16,210
We'll attack the heathens
as long as we breathe.

236
00:32:16,390 --> 00:32:20,740
We'll kill cruel people as
long as we breathe.

237
00:32:21,000 --> 00:32:27,230
Until we keep the Islam
flag flying.

238
00:32:27,270 --> 00:32:29,630
Yes, Bey.

239
00:32:29,750 --> 00:32:34,100
Flags will fly as you say so, Osman Bey!

240
00:32:37,060 --> 00:32:40,590
- Can I come in, my Bey?
- Come in.

241
00:33:02,920 --> 00:33:08,100
My Bey, they will move the next day.

242
00:33:08,570 --> 00:33:10,240
We are waiting for your command.

243
00:33:14,390 --> 00:33:15,750
The council is over.

244
00:33:16,730 --> 00:33:18,770
Everyone go back to your work.

245
00:33:19,800 --> 00:33:21,730
May it be easy.

246
00:33:58,840 --> 00:34:01,240
What did Osman bey read?

247
00:34:01,570 --> 00:34:04,530
He ended the council.

248
00:34:06,100 --> 00:34:09,600
We can't know.

249
00:34:11,400 --> 00:34:16,230
We can't figure out either.

250
00:34:16,679 --> 00:34:18,590
Yes...

251
00:34:19,440 --> 00:34:21,989
it must be important.

252
00:34:25,360 --> 00:34:27,469
It's from Konur.

253
00:34:27,980 --> 00:34:29,900
It's about Constantinople.

254
00:34:30,940 --> 00:34:35,340
People who want to
dethrone the Emperor took action.

255
00:34:37,659 --> 00:34:41,830
Emperor being on the throne
helps our conquests.

256
00:34:43,679 --> 00:34:47,380
Get ready.
We're going to Constantinople.

257
00:34:56,280 --> 00:35:00,210
My valiants. What are your duties?

258
00:35:07,960 --> 00:35:10,330
My brother is responsible for Karacahisar.

259
00:35:11,240 --> 00:35:12,780
Mashallah.

260
00:35:13,550 --> 00:35:16,680
Mashallah, my son.

261
00:35:18,850 --> 00:35:20,680
Mashallah.

262
00:35:23,290 --> 00:35:25,330
Mashallah, my brother!

263
00:35:33,480 --> 00:35:34,770
So, my Alaaddin?

264
00:35:35,170 --> 00:35:36,850
What is your duty?

265
00:35:44,020 --> 00:35:45,310
I don't have any.

266
00:35:48,540 --> 00:35:50,180
I don't have any duty.

267
00:36:01,050 --> 00:36:02,500
Don't say that, brother.

268
00:36:03,450 --> 00:36:07,290
Our father wants you to be good
for the state that he'll establish.

269
00:36:09,140 --> 00:36:10,550
You're right, my brother.

270
00:36:11,360 --> 00:36:12,990
Osman Bey said so.

271
00:36:38,530 --> 00:36:41,930
Get ready, Alps.

272
00:36:42,900 --> 00:36:44,700
We're going to enemy lands.

273
00:36:45,040 --> 00:36:47,450
We know them well, my Bey.

274
00:36:48,040 --> 00:36:50,620
We'll get through it.

275
00:36:51,750 --> 00:36:52,890
Yes, Kutan.

276
00:36:53,200 --> 00:36:55,190
Come on, it's time.

277
00:37:00,070 --> 00:37:02,830
You're ready, Alps.
Mashallah.

278
00:37:03,730 --> 00:37:05,320
Your food is here.

279
00:37:26,220 --> 00:37:27,250
Cerkutay.

280
00:37:31,660 --> 00:37:33,590
The biggest meal is yours.

281
00:37:35,910 --> 00:37:38,840
I'm not hungry.
I won't eat it.

282
00:37:39,570 --> 00:37:42,520
You will. You should.

283
00:37:43,820 --> 00:37:46,310
I said I'm not hungry.

284
00:37:49,040 --> 00:37:51,490
I won't eat. Don't you hear me?

285
00:37:51,690 --> 00:37:53,240
I'm full.

286
00:37:56,330 --> 00:37:59,400
Okay. I made fried meat.

287
00:38:01,890 --> 00:38:03,240
So much.

288
00:38:04,370 --> 00:38:06,270
There is calf's tongue in it.

289
00:38:07,040 --> 00:38:10,500
I'll take it back.

290
00:38:20,520 --> 00:38:22,400
I'm going back, Cerkutay.

291
00:38:23,180 --> 00:38:24,400
Won't you take it?

292
00:38:29,910 --> 00:38:36,360
I can't go there hungry.

293
00:38:36,460 --> 00:38:41,010
Yes! Eat it so you can fight the enemy.

294
00:38:50,450 --> 00:38:51,450
Cerkutay.

295
00:38:52,610 --> 00:38:53,410
Come on.

296
00:39:01,840 --> 00:39:06,400
My name is Cerkutay.

297
00:39:07,500 --> 00:39:10,240
Cer-ku-tay.

298
00:39:11,640 --> 00:39:12,620
Yes.

299
00:39:16,620 --> 00:39:18,910
Yes. I said so.

300
00:39:19,960 --> 00:39:22,480
Cer-gu-day.

301
00:39:26,590 --> 00:39:28,000
Eat.

302
00:39:28,390 --> 00:39:30,000
You should eat.

303
00:39:30,490 --> 00:39:31,330
You should.

304
00:39:32,820 --> 00:39:35,470
I can stay hungry but you should eat.

305
00:39:40,890 --> 00:39:42,770
I sent you on so many expeditions.

306
00:39:43,790 --> 00:39:46,360
It feels like the first time every time.

307
00:39:47,750 --> 00:39:49,790
Our enemies increase every day.

308
00:39:52,240 --> 00:39:54,010
Our expeditions increase.

309
00:39:54,420 --> 00:39:55,750
We grow, thank Allah.

310
00:39:57,220 --> 00:39:58,740
So is our children.

311
00:39:59,460 --> 00:40:01,360
They even attended their first council.

312
00:40:01,740 --> 00:40:03,930
Mashallah.

313
00:40:05,060 --> 00:40:07,020
They grow up.

314
00:40:10,770 --> 00:40:11,570
My Bey.

315
00:40:13,570 --> 00:40:14,730
I want to...

316
00:40:16,040 --> 00:40:17,760
say something.

317
00:40:22,450 --> 00:40:23,490
Tell me, my Bala.

318
00:40:27,080 --> 00:40:27,960
Tell me.

319
00:40:36,100 --> 00:40:37,240
May Allah speed you.

320
00:40:38,510 --> 00:40:41,390
I was going to say "May Allah speed you."

321
00:40:42,190 --> 00:40:43,880
May Allah help you.

322
00:40:45,020 --> 00:40:46,330
May you succeed.

323
00:41:04,530 --> 00:41:05,690
Thank you.

324
00:42:16,080 --> 00:42:17,380
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim.

325
00:42:18,320 --> 00:42:20,360
Alps!
Come on!

326
00:43:19,880 --> 00:43:22,950
My Alaaddin didn't seem good.
How's he?

327
00:43:23,660 --> 00:43:25,110
He was offended.

328
00:43:25,630 --> 00:43:27,250
However, he'll be fine.

329
00:43:27,350 --> 00:43:28,430
Inshallah.

330
00:43:28,810 --> 00:43:30,790
Don't worry, my Bala.

331
00:43:31,240 --> 00:43:33,550
Osman Bey knows what he's doing.

332
00:43:34,240 --> 00:43:36,100
Alaaddin will understand it.

333
00:43:38,820 --> 00:43:40,010
What will we do now?

334
00:43:40,950 --> 00:43:42,560
I might go to the bazaar.

335
00:43:42,870 --> 00:43:44,970
Today, the goods will be there.

336
00:43:45,440 --> 00:43:46,340
Okay, then.

337
00:43:46,530 --> 00:43:49,190
We'll go and check the
goods for the bazaar.

338
00:43:49,330 --> 00:43:51,860
We should check them.

339
00:43:52,410 --> 00:43:53,900
Good.

340
00:43:54,800 --> 00:43:55,900
Come on.

341
00:43:56,800 --> 00:43:57,650
May it be easy.

342
00:43:58,080 --> 00:43:58,970
May it be easy.

343
00:43:59,450 --> 00:44:00,410
Come on, Hatuns.

344
00:44:02,220 --> 00:44:04,580
Constantinople

345
00:44:36,970 --> 00:44:38,400
I don't want any trouble.

346
00:44:49,190 --> 00:44:53,370
Tomorrow, the sun will rise in Rome again.

347
00:45:16,510 --> 00:45:18,760
This is the boat we'll use, my Bey.

348
00:45:30,690 --> 00:45:33,350
We will arrive in
Constantinople before noon.

349
00:45:33,910 --> 00:45:37,280
We should be careful.

350
00:45:37,880 --> 00:45:39,140
May our war be holy.

351
00:45:39,160 --> 00:45:40,710
Amin.

352
00:46:13,430 --> 00:46:15,480
Öktem Tent

353
00:46:22,260 --> 00:46:25,390
Thank you, Hatuns.
The cheese is delicious.

354
00:46:27,550 --> 00:46:30,440
Let's check the saddles
before Bengi Hatun comes, Aktemur.

355
00:47:03,180 --> 00:47:04,780
It doesn't look fine.

356
00:47:06,410 --> 00:47:08,130
Let's look at it on the horse.

357
00:47:11,510 --> 00:47:12,840
It's thin.

358
00:47:13,490 --> 00:47:15,920
It should be thick so it will absorb
horse's sweat.

359
00:47:19,100 --> 00:47:20,490
Where is Bengi Hatun?

360
00:47:20,870 --> 00:47:22,490
Didn't you tell her we came?

361
00:47:22,680 --> 00:47:24,020
We did but...

362
00:47:24,720 --> 00:47:26,720
Welcome, Malhun Hatun.

363
00:47:29,780 --> 00:47:31,170
Sorry.

364
00:47:32,280 --> 00:47:37,010
We'd welcome you better if we knew
earlier that you were coming.

365
00:47:38,390 --> 00:47:41,020
Come, drink our Ayran.

366
00:47:41,240 --> 00:47:42,420
Thank you.

367
00:47:43,780 --> 00:47:45,230
We're not here to sit.

368
00:47:45,510 --> 00:47:48,340
We're here to check the
goods for the bazaar.

369
00:47:49,380 --> 00:47:53,370
However, we don't like what we see.

370
00:48:12,950 --> 00:48:14,870
What is this saddle?

371
00:48:15,350 --> 00:48:17,700
Why don't you like it, Malhun Hatun?

372
00:48:18,670 --> 00:48:20,120
It's the same.

373
00:48:20,540 --> 00:48:22,530
It can't stand in balance on the horse.

374
00:48:22,790 --> 00:48:25,430
How can I send this to the bazaar
when I can't even...

375
00:48:25,470 --> 00:48:26,790
let my Alps ride this?

376
00:48:27,290 --> 00:48:28,500
Malhun Hatun!

377
00:48:34,300 --> 00:48:35,190
Alçiçek.

378
00:48:41,780 --> 00:48:43,840
Give me your best Alp.

379
00:48:45,110 --> 00:48:50,580
So that I can show him how to ride a horse
with the saddle you don't like.

380
00:48:55,810 --> 00:48:57,380
No need, girl.

381
00:49:17,660 --> 00:49:19,300
Can I, Malhun Hatun?

382
00:49:31,320 --> 00:49:32,640
Follow me.

383
00:49:33,620 --> 00:49:35,940
There's a big tree outside the tent.

384
00:49:36,060 --> 00:49:37,450
We will race from there.

385
00:49:40,950 --> 00:49:41,780
Come on!

386
00:49:50,030 --> 00:49:51,210
Come on!

387
00:49:56,680 --> 00:49:57,780
Come on!

388
00:50:13,480 --> 00:50:15,920
Show me your talent.

389
00:50:17,510 --> 00:50:19,660
Tell me your name before I win.

390
00:50:20,080 --> 00:50:21,800
I want to know who I will defeat.

391
00:50:23,280 --> 00:50:25,000
Aktemur, son of Gündüz Bey.

392
00:50:28,890 --> 00:50:30,120
Thank you, Temur Bey.

393
00:50:33,470 --> 00:50:35,100
Come on!

394
00:51:16,320 --> 00:51:17,070
Come on!

395
00:51:20,300 --> 00:51:21,110
Come on!

396
00:51:42,550 --> 00:51:44,330
Mashallah. my daughter.

397
00:51:45,850 --> 00:51:47,050
She's good.

398
00:52:06,740 --> 00:52:08,390
See, Malhun Hatun?

399
00:52:08,880 --> 00:52:12,830
I defeated your Alp
on the saddle you don't like.

400
00:52:15,410 --> 00:52:17,890
I see, Alçiçek.
I see.

401
00:52:18,400 --> 00:52:21,190
Mashallah. You're good at it.

402
00:52:22,790 --> 00:52:25,410
However, you're callow.

403
00:52:26,060 --> 00:52:31,610
You don't even see the wound of the horse.

404
00:52:40,510 --> 00:52:44,130
This is why Aktemur fell behind.

405
00:52:53,490 --> 00:52:56,050
A horse is Alp's wing during the war.

406
00:52:58,210 --> 00:53:00,970
What happens when that wing breaks?

407
00:53:12,960 --> 00:53:16,440
Constantinople

408
00:53:18,320 --> 00:53:20,810
Constantinople!

409
00:53:41,010 --> 00:53:46,070
Brother, would you want to hear azan here?

410
00:53:47,040 --> 00:53:48,640
Inshallah, brother.

411
00:53:49,410 --> 00:53:51,240
This is the best wish.

412
00:53:53,040 --> 00:53:55,120
This is what war is for.

413
00:54:00,870 --> 00:54:06,270
If we try and unite, we will
hear azan here.

414
00:54:09,010 --> 00:54:11,320
Look at the moon.

415
00:54:12,320 --> 00:54:14,750
It's above the cross.

416
00:54:15,670 --> 00:54:21,750
If Muslims unite after this flag...

417
00:54:23,040 --> 00:54:30,240
the azan will be heard not just in
Hagia Sophia, in everywhere.

418
00:54:47,240 --> 00:54:48,900
Welcome, my Bey.

419
00:54:50,100 --> 00:54:51,580
Thank you.

420
00:54:54,270 --> 00:54:55,640
It's ready.

421
00:54:55,990 --> 00:54:57,560
This way.

422
00:55:22,180 --> 00:55:25,300
Welcome to Constantinople, Osman.

423
00:55:30,270 --> 00:55:32,580
Öktem Tent

424
00:55:41,810 --> 00:55:43,550
Oh, Hatun...

425
00:55:44,150 --> 00:55:46,610
why is this anger for?

426
00:55:48,440 --> 00:55:53,870
Do you want to cripple my leg again?

427
00:55:56,180 --> 00:55:58,920
My mother is angry at Malhun Hatun.

428
00:55:59,380 --> 00:56:02,900
As Malhun Hatun is in a
palace, not in a tent...

429
00:56:03,210 --> 00:56:04,900
she's showing off.

430
00:56:05,420 --> 00:56:08,170
She reprehended me in front
of my people and in my tent.

431
00:56:08,280 --> 00:56:09,520
How dare she?

432
00:56:11,270 --> 00:56:12,640
Why?

433
00:56:13,120 --> 00:56:14,640
She said our goods are bad.

434
00:56:15,920 --> 00:56:17,950
What is bad?

435
00:56:18,300 --> 00:56:20,720
If she wants to find it bad, she can.

436
00:56:23,580 --> 00:56:27,780
She said saddles hurt the animals.

437
00:56:28,210 --> 00:56:30,630
My Bey.
Batur Alp and Bayındır Alp is here.

438
00:56:31,120 --> 00:56:33,210
Let them in.

439
00:56:36,120 --> 00:56:37,040
Hatun.

440
00:56:37,670 --> 00:56:39,320
Look at me.

441
00:56:39,920 --> 00:56:44,550
Osman Bey really cares about the
bazaar and the goods in it.

442
00:56:44,870 --> 00:56:46,550
He checks everything.

443
00:56:47,640 --> 00:56:51,240
Send the best goods to the bazaar.

444
00:57:42,610 --> 00:57:44,070
This way, my Bey.

445
00:58:15,350 --> 00:58:19,530
So, Osman Bey wants you to send
Alps to Karaağaç.

446
00:58:21,980 --> 00:58:23,950
It's close to Makli, I get it...

447
00:58:23,950 --> 00:58:25,950
I do but...

448
00:58:26,120 --> 00:58:29,410
I don't know why he sends Alps to there.

449
00:58:29,840 --> 00:58:33,550
You only hear what you want to hear.

450
00:58:33,840 --> 00:58:36,120
Didn't he say in the council that...

451
00:58:36,120 --> 00:58:40,810
Karaağaç is the heathens' neighbor and
Marmaracık is important?

452
00:58:41,550 --> 00:58:43,740
He did.

453
00:58:44,300 --> 00:58:47,360
Then you gave a duty to Batur.

454
00:58:48,180 --> 00:58:50,150
You should have gone there.

455
00:58:50,550 --> 00:58:52,120
I would.

456
00:58:53,550 --> 00:58:56,720
What I bought must have
discouraged you, Bayındır.

457
00:59:01,320 --> 00:59:04,560
I don't become satisfied.

458
00:59:05,010 --> 00:59:07,050
Send your Alps, Ökten Bey...

459
00:59:07,100 --> 00:59:10,840
so that the conquest will happen
and we will have money.

460
00:59:12,350 --> 00:59:16,010
Your love for loot is more
than your love for war.

461
00:59:21,380 --> 00:59:23,300
- Batur.
- Yes, my Bey.

462
00:59:23,950 --> 00:59:25,580
The duty is yours.

463
00:59:27,300 --> 00:59:28,980
Karaağaç is ours.

464
00:59:29,250 --> 00:59:30,590
Makli belongs to heathens.

465
00:59:31,640 --> 00:59:35,120
However, protect it like
it's your own land.

466
00:59:36,810 --> 00:59:39,830
If Osman Bey told to send Alps there...

467
00:59:39,920 --> 00:59:41,880
he must have felt something.

468
00:59:41,920 --> 00:59:43,490
Be careful.

469
00:59:43,530 --> 00:59:47,320
Your command, my Bey.
I take the road in the morning.

470
00:59:48,470 --> 00:59:50,320
My valiant brother.

471
00:59:50,920 --> 00:59:53,810
He will do his duty appropriately.

472
01:00:18,350 --> 01:00:20,100
Tell us, Konur.

473
01:00:21,150 --> 01:00:22,750
The palace is there.

474
01:00:23,980 --> 01:00:25,720
The arena is there.

475
01:00:27,700 --> 01:00:30,350
Commander Sen Tahor should be the one.

476
01:00:30,480 --> 01:00:32,480
However, we don't know what it is.

477
01:00:34,150 --> 01:00:36,100
We should learn.

478
01:00:36,720 --> 01:00:40,520
They will talk tomorrow.

479
01:00:42,120 --> 01:00:46,900
However, you will check the slaves.

480
01:00:47,350 --> 01:00:49,440
When we protect the Emperor...

481
01:00:50,150 --> 01:00:53,660
you will send those slaves and make
them attack Sen Tahor's soldiers.

482
01:00:53,920 --> 01:00:55,920
Your command, my Bey.

483
01:01:04,950 --> 01:01:06,780
Emperor will sit here.

484
01:01:08,410 --> 01:01:09,950
This seat is for you, my Bey.

485
01:01:10,110 --> 01:01:12,110
It's close to Emperor.

486
01:01:13,270 --> 01:01:14,270
Then...

487
01:01:16,870 --> 01:01:18,500
Boran will be behind me.

488
01:01:19,010 --> 01:01:20,470
Yes, my Bey.

489
01:01:22,440 --> 01:01:24,240
You...

490
01:01:26,100 --> 01:01:27,870
will be right in front of me.

491
01:01:38,290 --> 01:01:40,130
Tell me.

492
01:01:40,500 --> 01:01:42,240
Are they ready to support me?

493
01:01:42,860 --> 01:01:45,720
Vatican will support the person
who will revive Rome.

494
01:01:46,060 --> 01:01:47,720
You tell me. Are you ready?

495
01:01:49,240 --> 01:01:51,580
Always.

496
01:01:51,720 --> 01:01:54,640
Emperor will die in the arena tomorrow.

497
01:01:56,220 --> 01:01:57,900
Rome will revive.

498
01:01:58,600 --> 01:02:00,700
Turks nightmare is about to begin.

499
01:02:01,150 --> 01:02:02,700
How will it happen?

500
01:02:06,950 --> 01:02:08,950
Commander Sen Tahor.

501
01:02:09,470 --> 01:02:12,570
A real soldier who
wants the best for Rome.

502
01:02:15,010 --> 01:02:17,180
He will serve us in the arena.

503
01:02:19,410 --> 01:02:22,870
I greet you with respect, Cardinal.

504
01:02:24,970 --> 01:02:26,590
If you want our support...

505
01:02:26,680 --> 01:02:28,650
we should see you have the throne.

506
01:02:28,810 --> 01:02:33,300
Then, we will give you the power
you want, Kantakuzenos.

507
01:02:33,350 --> 01:02:37,670
I won't stop until I take
the lands from Osman back.

508
01:02:38,300 --> 01:02:40,010
I give you victory.

509
01:03:16,920 --> 01:03:18,350
Son.

510
01:03:32,180 --> 01:03:33,690
Are you fine, my Aladdin?

511
01:03:40,320 --> 01:03:41,410
Mother.

512
01:03:43,640 --> 01:03:45,980
I can't fight as my brother does.

513
01:03:47,700 --> 01:03:49,380
I am not strong like my father.

514
01:03:50,980 --> 01:03:53,520
I seem weak and clumsy.

515
01:03:57,980 --> 01:04:02,810
No one will listen to me, will they?

516
01:04:06,610 --> 01:04:07,920
You're wrong, my valiant.

517
01:04:08,840 --> 01:04:09,920
You're wrong.

518
01:04:13,950 --> 01:04:17,980
Look.
Look at your five fingers.

519
01:04:18,610 --> 01:04:20,580
They are all different, right?

520
01:04:20,580 --> 01:04:23,150
They have all different roles.

521
01:04:24,580 --> 01:04:26,670
Also, you are a decent fighter.

522
01:04:27,520 --> 01:04:29,380
Why are you thinking like this?

523
01:04:31,470 --> 01:04:32,470
No.

524
01:04:33,100 --> 01:04:34,270
I am not, mother.

525
01:04:36,700 --> 01:04:38,900
My brother always defeats me.

526
01:04:40,500 --> 01:04:42,980
He wins every duel between us.

527
01:04:43,810 --> 01:04:46,260
I can't defeat him
no matter how hard I try.

528
01:04:47,670 --> 01:04:49,040
I am weak.

529
01:04:50,270 --> 01:04:51,670
Look at me.

530
01:04:53,440 --> 01:04:56,750
You are neither weak nor clumsy.

531
01:04:57,550 --> 01:05:03,810
Power comes from bravery, which is
standing against the cruels, son.

532
01:05:04,870 --> 01:05:10,180
Strength doesn't come from arms.
It comes from here.

533
01:05:10,180 --> 01:05:12,180
Then why...

534
01:05:13,040 --> 01:05:15,750
...my father didn't give me a mission?

535
01:05:17,010 --> 01:05:19,550
What do I lack
that my brother doesn't, mother?

536
01:05:26,150 --> 01:05:28,350
Do you envy your brother?

537
01:05:43,380 --> 01:05:46,270
I was going to give my brother a gift...

538
01:05:47,580 --> 01:05:49,410
But it turns out he just envies me...

539
01:05:50,810 --> 01:05:52,390
...Instead of appreciating me.

540
01:05:54,550 --> 01:05:56,300
I don't envy him, mother.

541
01:05:57,440 --> 01:06:00,500
That my brother receives roles
makes me happy the most.

542
01:06:02,640 --> 01:06:06,150
I just want to know what I lack.

543
01:06:08,610 --> 01:06:10,610
My father doesn't trust me, mother.

544
01:06:11,070 --> 01:06:13,270
He thinks I am weak.

545
01:06:14,720 --> 01:06:17,780
I know it.
This is why he doesn't give me roles.

546
01:06:18,640 --> 01:06:20,240
Aladdin.

547
01:06:21,440 --> 01:06:23,520
Son, Aladdin!

548
01:06:43,310 --> 01:06:46,500
Constantinople

549
01:07:19,250 --> 01:07:22,080
Not only fighters will bleed today.

550
01:07:22,350 --> 01:07:24,500
They have a game here.

551
01:07:25,070 --> 01:07:30,240
And we have come a long way to
ruin their game.

552
01:07:31,700 --> 01:07:33,070
Let's go.

553
01:07:48,210 --> 01:07:49,840
Hello Ürgen Hatun!

554
01:07:49,840 --> 01:07:51,840
Hello to you!

555
01:07:51,840 --> 01:07:53,840
Leave it there.

556
01:08:02,320 --> 01:08:05,020
Now it's your chance to show your skills,
Kayi Alp.

557
01:08:05,020 --> 01:08:07,530
Tell me your name before
I kick you under the dust.

558
01:08:07,530 --> 01:08:09,210
Gunduz Bey's son Aktemur.

559
01:08:16,439 --> 01:08:18,240
Keep blending.

560
01:08:26,720 --> 01:08:30,460
You have been playing with your meal.
Will you ever eat?

561
01:08:33,840 --> 01:08:36,350
Tell me now, what's wrong my Bey?

562
01:08:36,350 --> 01:08:38,350
Nothing wrong, Ürgen Hatun.

563
01:08:39,120 --> 01:08:43,149
Is it because of yesterday's defeat?

564
01:08:45,500 --> 01:08:48,149
I heard that Alcicek beat you.

565
01:08:48,580 --> 01:08:50,350
Help me understand.

566
01:08:50,410 --> 01:08:55,899
Aktemur Bey, who defeated countless Alps,
is defeated by a tiny girl. Is this right?

567
01:08:55,899 --> 01:08:57,899
It was more like a give up for her.

568
01:08:57,899 --> 01:08:59,640
She was very eager.

569
01:08:59,640 --> 01:09:03,840
I didn't want to upset her.
Or I would...

570
01:09:04,350 --> 01:09:05,550
Or what?

571
01:09:07,040 --> 01:09:09,439
- Or you are in love!
- Ürgen Hatun!

572
01:09:11,180 --> 01:09:12,979
What are you talking about?

573
01:09:15,100 --> 01:09:17,538
There is no such thing as
"love at first sight"

574
01:09:19,779 --> 01:09:22,220
I don't even know
if she loves someone or not.

575
01:09:22,979 --> 01:09:25,840
So you say she is for you
if her heart is empty.

576
01:09:28,069 --> 01:09:29,340
Yes.

577
01:09:41,810 --> 01:09:43,640
May your path be clear, my Orhan.

578
01:09:44,180 --> 01:09:45,720
May my Creator protect you.

579
01:10:20,670 --> 01:10:22,570
You have been a good sister to me.

580
01:10:22,610 --> 01:10:24,980
This is for you.
Protect yourself while I'm gone.

581
01:10:24,980 --> 01:10:27,870
Brother, this is your favourite dagger!

582
01:10:27,980 --> 01:10:30,470
So you're just giving it to me?
Thank you!

583
01:10:49,270 --> 01:10:51,210
You are entrusted to Allah.

584
01:10:53,710 --> 01:10:56,000
You too, son.

585
01:11:27,100 --> 01:11:28,220
Alps!

586
01:11:28,750 --> 01:11:30,200
Awaken!

587
01:11:30,410 --> 01:11:32,010
As you order, my Bey!

588
01:11:32,380 --> 01:11:33,580
Let's go!

589
01:11:48,650 --> 01:11:50,180
Praise be!

590
01:11:50,860 --> 01:11:52,930
We witnessed him become a Bey.

591
01:11:53,460 --> 01:11:56,410
May my Creator let us witness
having a grandchild as well.

592
01:11:57,620 --> 01:11:59,810
Amen, my Ayse.
Amen.

593
01:12:01,740 --> 01:12:04,280
You always take it to the bride somehow,
Ayse.

594
01:12:05,480 --> 01:12:07,380
You are talking about Orhan...

595
01:12:08,530 --> 01:12:10,780
...but you want Aktemur to hear as well.
Right?

596
01:12:14,350 --> 01:12:17,740
I want him to hear but
he just doesn't listen, Bala.

597
01:12:18,630 --> 01:12:20,570
He won't hear me.

598
01:12:28,950 --> 01:12:34,590
Constantinople.

599
01:13:08,930 --> 01:13:10,820
Great Rome!

600
01:14:53,490 --> 01:14:57,100
Kill him! Kill!

601
01:16:44,220 --> 01:16:46,180
People of Holy Rome!

602
01:16:48,850 --> 01:16:53,270
Supreme Emperor Andrikos' Gladiator Games
is about to start!

603
01:16:59,710 --> 01:17:01,310
They were born to kill.

604
01:17:01,530 --> 01:17:03,110
The most noble warriors.

605
01:17:04,610 --> 01:17:06,530
Rufuz the axe of death!

606
01:17:11,660 --> 01:17:13,860
Diko the shield!

607
01:17:21,000 --> 01:17:22,900
Slaves from birth!

608
01:17:25,090 --> 01:17:26,920
Fight for your freedom!

609
01:18:00,390 --> 01:18:05,790
Kill! Kill! Kill!

610
01:18:17,790 --> 01:18:19,360
Hey, you!

611
01:18:20,280 --> 01:18:21,720
Why don't you cheer!?

612
01:18:24,510 --> 01:18:28,850
"If you stayed silent...

613
01:18:31,290 --> 01:18:33,350
...you would be a philosopher.

614
01:18:42,620 --> 01:18:44,140
What was that, Cerkutay?

615
01:18:44,530 --> 01:18:45,510
What did you say?

616
01:18:45,680 --> 01:18:48,450
I said "Silent horses kick hard"

617
01:18:50,960 --> 01:18:52,760
Not exactly this line, but...

618
01:18:53,440 --> 01:18:55,300
...something like that, I guess.

619
01:18:55,300 --> 01:18:57,170
It worked.
That's what matters now.

620
01:18:58,390 --> 01:18:59,990
It'll start soon.

621
01:19:00,360 --> 01:19:01,760
Get ready.

622
01:19:03,130 --> 01:19:14,210
Long live Emperor!
Long live Emperor!

623
01:19:19,150 --> 01:19:22,070
You'll cheer my name at the end of the day.

624
01:19:23,360 --> 01:19:33,100
Long live Emperor!
Long live Emperor!

625
01:19:36,650 --> 01:19:39,260
Removed shows came back!

626
01:19:40,080 --> 01:19:41,000
Why?

627
01:19:41,190 --> 01:19:45,200
Because Rome needs to be ready for a war.

628
01:19:46,660 --> 01:19:52,680
Rome's might will come back just like
this removed show!

629
01:20:46,840 --> 01:20:49,810
The fight shall begin!

630
01:21:03,110 --> 01:21:04,710
You play games.

631
01:21:06,480 --> 01:21:08,980
You shed blood for fun.

632
01:22:04,110 --> 01:22:06,880
The traitor went in.

633
01:22:08,360 --> 01:22:18,560
Kill! Kill! Kill!

634
01:22:22,200 --> 01:22:26,320
Emperor Andranikos will kneel!

635
01:22:27,890 --> 01:22:33,270
And everyone who supports him will die.

636
01:22:34,420 --> 01:22:38,360
I need brave men!

637
01:22:42,640 --> 01:22:48,380
We will bleed for Rome today!

638
01:22:55,230 --> 01:22:56,780
My soldiers!

639
01:22:59,260 --> 01:23:04,880
In Rome, the sun will rise again today!

640
01:23:05,500 --> 01:23:08,460
- For Rome!
- For Rome!

641
01:23:08,580 --> 01:23:13,800
- For Rome!
- For Rome!

642
01:23:59,950 --> 01:24:02,320
Come on commander, where are you?

643
01:24:10,110 --> 01:24:14,930
Here is the real commander of Rome,
Sen Tahor!

644
01:24:16,820 --> 01:24:33,010
Kill! Kill! Kill!

645
01:26:55,080 --> 01:26:57,220
Get out of my way!

646
01:26:58,780 --> 01:27:00,220
What's happening!

647
01:27:11,010 --> 01:27:12,500
Protect the emperor!

648
01:27:18,870 --> 01:27:21,290
Emperor Andranikos!

649
01:27:21,420 --> 01:27:23,630
The throne belongs to the brave!

650
01:27:23,780 --> 01:27:26,120
Soldiers! Attack!

651
01:27:50,740 --> 01:27:51,620
Boran!

652
01:27:51,620 --> 01:27:53,190
- I'm here my Bey!
- Off we go!

653
01:29:07,950 --> 01:29:09,480
You traitor!

654
01:29:09,790 --> 01:29:12,330
How dare you!

655
01:30:21,420 --> 01:30:23,040
Boran!

656
01:31:55,260 --> 01:31:56,450
Osman Bey

657
01:31:56,940 --> 01:31:59,860
You learn how to howl
when you have a wolf friend.

658
01:32:03,020 --> 01:32:05,220
Come with me, Emperor.

659
01:32:05,990 --> 01:32:07,560
Emperor!

660
01:32:17,260 --> 01:32:19,530
I will save you, Emperor.

661
01:32:19,640 --> 01:32:21,600
How are we going to get out, Osman Bey?

662
01:32:21,600 --> 01:32:22,500
Emperor!

663
01:32:24,970 --> 01:32:25,840
Come on.

664
01:32:26,120 --> 01:32:26,910
No.

665
01:32:27,100 --> 01:32:28,970
Come on now!

666
01:32:45,340 --> 01:32:46,580
My Bey!

667
01:32:52,890 --> 01:32:54,730
Are you fine, brother?

668
01:33:14,140 --> 01:33:15,780
You're fine, right?

669
01:33:15,890 --> 01:33:19,020
I am. I have just become a Ghazi.

670
01:33:34,170 --> 01:33:35,390
My Bey!

671
01:33:43,290 --> 01:33:46,990
We are with you until the
reinforcement arrives, Emperor.

672
01:33:47,100 --> 01:33:47,880
Okay.

673
01:33:51,980 --> 01:33:52,780
Come on.

674
01:34:18,720 --> 01:34:20,720
Protect the Emperor!

675
01:34:21,180 --> 01:34:23,610
Protect the Emperor!

676
01:34:37,760 --> 01:34:39,530
Sentor!

677
01:34:42,360 --> 01:34:47,200
Kantakuzenos!
You low dog!

678
01:34:57,690 --> 01:35:03,890
You betrayed our plan, Kantakuzenos!

679
01:35:04,500 --> 01:35:06,700
Calm down, Sen Tahor.

680
01:35:06,870 --> 01:35:08,960
I will save you from this situation.

681
01:35:09,160 --> 01:35:12,160
You will let me go.

682
01:35:12,390 --> 01:35:15,530
Or I will crush you!

683
01:35:17,060 --> 01:35:19,100
Don't let that ignoble run away, alps.

684
01:35:24,090 --> 01:35:25,910
Kantakuzenos!

685
01:35:26,260 --> 01:35:30,490
You will not talk and I will
get you out of dungeon.

686
01:35:35,130 --> 01:35:36,830
You're late.

687
01:35:39,080 --> 01:35:41,360
I just caught the traitor.

688
01:35:42,110 --> 01:35:44,410
Let's take him to the emperor.

689
01:35:52,800 --> 01:35:54,200
Let's do it.

690
01:35:55,400 --> 01:35:56,700
Come on.

691
01:36:13,580 --> 01:36:15,980
Hang on, valiants!

692
01:36:16,130 --> 01:36:20,040
Neither we nor your valiants have
no power left to hang on, Osman Bey!

693
01:36:20,640 --> 01:36:25,740
We can hang on
but where are your soldiers?

694
01:36:25,940 --> 01:36:28,920
The attackers must have moved them away.

695
01:36:29,600 --> 01:36:32,030
They should be here soon!

696
01:38:34,820 --> 01:38:36,370
Dog!

697
01:38:36,820 --> 01:38:38,550
Who is behind you!

698
01:38:38,770 --> 01:38:40,330
Tell me!

699
01:38:46,560 --> 01:38:51,740
You can't escape your death
even if you figure that out.

700
01:38:54,650 --> 01:38:59,730
The throne belongs to its real owner.

701
01:39:00,680 --> 01:39:02,660
You will talk.

702
01:39:03,160 --> 01:39:04,730
Take him to the dungeon!

703
01:39:05,140 --> 01:39:09,570
Beat him up so that he speaks.

704
01:39:24,560 --> 01:39:29,370
Osman Bey, I want to host you in my Palace.

705
01:39:32,170 --> 01:39:34,430
It's good that you invited us.

706
01:39:36,230 --> 01:39:39,010
We were not invited while
we were on our way here.

707
01:39:44,260 --> 01:39:47,220
Come on. Let's go.

708
01:39:52,750 --> 01:39:54,100
Good.

709
01:40:21,810 --> 01:40:27,750
Did you really give us the remotest place
of the bazaar, Ayse Hatun?

710
01:40:28,020 --> 01:40:30,830
Not at all, Bengu Hatun.

711
01:40:30,980 --> 01:40:33,230
The stalls are separated
according to the goods.

712
01:40:33,380 --> 01:40:35,280
And this is your place.

713
01:40:35,430 --> 01:40:37,490
I don't want this stall.

714
01:40:37,890 --> 01:40:40,130
Is this what you give us
in return of everything we did?

715
01:40:40,130 --> 01:40:42,420
Give us one of the first stalls
at the enterance.

716
01:40:43,170 --> 01:40:44,800
Hatuns!

717
01:40:52,010 --> 01:40:54,480
What is happening here, Hatuns?

718
01:40:55,340 --> 01:40:57,860
Your voice reaches to the other end
of the bazaar.

719
01:41:00,240 --> 01:41:01,570
Well...

720
01:41:02,870 --> 01:41:07,400
...you gave the remotest, the most corner
place of the bazaar, Malhun Hatun.

721
01:41:09,030 --> 01:41:10,660
Bengu Hatun.

722
01:41:11,430 --> 01:41:15,490
We catagorise the bazaar according to the
type of goods.

723
01:41:15,660 --> 01:41:17,820
We do everything for you.

724
01:41:17,970 --> 01:41:19,820
Competition brings fruitfulness.

725
01:41:22,820 --> 01:41:28,050
Tell me about the saddles, Bengu Hatun.
I hope they're not like the last time I saw them.

726
01:41:36,320 --> 01:41:40,320
We completed the goods, Malhun Hatun.
There is no lackings.

727
01:41:45,580 --> 01:41:48,510
Alcicek. Bengu Hatun's daughter.

728
01:41:48,680 --> 01:41:50,640
Welcome.

729
01:41:54,090 --> 01:41:55,670
Unload them.

730
01:42:07,660 --> 01:42:10,040
Masha Allah! (praise be!)
Masha Allah! (praise be!)

731
01:42:29,490 --> 01:42:33,120
We trusted your words and came here.

732
01:42:34,570 --> 01:42:40,750
Who is going to visit this
fasty isolated place?

733
01:42:41,180 --> 01:42:43,910
Once in a blue moon.

734
01:43:08,240 --> 01:43:10,940
He set up a great bazaar, but...

735
01:43:11,520 --> 01:43:14,650
...who is going to come here?

736
01:43:15,280 --> 01:43:17,500
Who will buy all these?

737
01:43:18,830 --> 01:43:22,030
He sent a messenger to overseas, he says.

738
01:43:23,140 --> 01:43:27,090
Osman Bey must know something as
he set it up here.

739
01:43:27,640 --> 01:43:30,450
You are the one who says we must trust him.

740
01:43:30,600 --> 01:43:32,450
We must, but...

741
01:43:32,650 --> 01:43:35,880
...we need him to make us rich.

742
01:43:36,230 --> 01:43:37,810
Osman is hungry.

743
01:43:38,010 --> 01:43:40,660
He is like a child in a sweet shop.

744
01:43:42,090 --> 01:43:43,940
So you won't sell in this bazaar?

745
01:43:44,670 --> 01:43:52,280
Oktem Bey, I expect nothing
out of this bazaar, so I won't invest.

746
01:43:55,200 --> 01:43:57,830
Crafty you are!

747
01:43:59,060 --> 01:44:01,490
You would invest everything you have...

748
01:44:01,760 --> 01:44:04,640
...if you were sure this bazaar
would work.

749
01:44:09,750 --> 01:44:12,880
I am not saying anything else.

750
01:44:31,150 --> 01:44:33,260
Hey my brave soul brother.

751
01:44:33,580 --> 01:44:35,480
My mother's memorial.

752
01:44:35,930 --> 01:44:39,840
You visit many villages, but
you haven't found a bride yet.

753
01:44:41,040 --> 01:44:42,940
I will find one for you.

754
01:44:43,220 --> 01:44:44,550
I want to see you married.

755
01:44:44,700 --> 01:44:47,250
Don't think about these, sister.

756
01:44:47,430 --> 01:44:49,300
It's time to go now.

757
01:44:49,500 --> 01:44:51,130
Osman Bey commanded.

758
01:44:51,260 --> 01:44:55,160
We will protect the Makri borders
in the name of Oktem Bey

759
01:44:56,260 --> 01:44:57,510
Give me your blessings.

760
01:44:59,270 --> 01:45:01,870
I do, my valiant brother.

761
01:45:13,360 --> 01:45:14,390
Come here!

762
01:45:14,560 --> 01:45:16,040
Yes, my Bey?

763
01:45:16,290 --> 01:45:18,520
Follow Batur.

764
01:45:19,870 --> 01:45:24,380
We need to know what happens
in Osman's distribution of goods.

765
01:45:24,700 --> 01:45:26,850
Yes my Bey.

766
01:45:32,640 --> 01:45:36,090
Constantinie Emperor's Palace.

767
01:45:42,700 --> 01:45:43,620
Get out!

768
01:45:48,880 --> 01:45:50,480
Soldiers, get out!

769
01:46:02,740 --> 01:46:05,400
How did you know this was going to happen,
Osman Bey?

770
01:46:05,960 --> 01:46:08,160
What we already know doesn't matter.

771
01:46:10,140 --> 01:46:12,580
We are after what we don't know.

772
01:46:21,060 --> 01:46:23,220
Why would you do this for me?

773
01:46:25,740 --> 01:46:28,040
Why do you want me to
stay on the throne?

774
01:46:28,460 --> 01:46:32,020
Isn't an unexperienced emperor
better for you?

775
01:46:32,640 --> 01:46:34,080
Kantakuzeros.

776
01:46:34,080 --> 01:46:35,480
My daughter Ofelia.

777
01:46:35,480 --> 01:46:37,480
Or someone from the dynasty.

778
01:46:38,140 --> 01:46:40,300
We have been in war for a long time.

779
01:46:42,220 --> 01:46:44,740
We lost many valiants.

780
01:46:46,220 --> 01:46:48,700
You know the war very well, Andranikos.

781
01:46:50,420 --> 01:46:52,060
But...

782
01:46:54,020 --> 01:46:56,260
...your presence supports the peace.

783
01:46:58,820 --> 01:47:01,140
How unlucky I am to...

784
01:47:01,460 --> 01:47:03,920
...get attacked by my people...

785
01:47:04,300 --> 01:47:05,920
...and to be saved from my enemy.

786
01:47:07,200 --> 01:47:08,460
No.

787
01:47:09,360 --> 01:47:10,940
You are a lucky man.

788
01:47:13,680 --> 01:47:15,520
You have a friend like me.

789
01:47:21,340 --> 01:47:22,480
I appreciate that.

790
01:47:24,860 --> 01:47:26,160
But why?

791
01:47:26,800 --> 01:47:29,240
They could kill me in my bed
while I was sleeping.

792
01:47:29,240 --> 01:47:31,740
They want you to hand the merchant.

793
01:47:34,320 --> 01:47:36,840
A dead emperor only causes disorder.

794
01:47:38,060 --> 01:47:39,100
Now tell me.

795
01:47:39,560 --> 01:47:42,380
Who wanted your throne?

796
01:47:56,540 --> 01:47:58,840
If you give up on your strength...

797
01:48:00,940 --> 01:48:04,030
...there will be many more who
set their eyes on your throne.

798
01:48:05,500 --> 01:48:06,940
But if you stay strong...

799
01:48:07,200 --> 01:48:09,480
...nobody will dare.

800
01:48:11,820 --> 01:48:12,640
Strength...

801
01:48:16,460 --> 01:48:17,920
...comes from trade.

802
01:48:25,680 --> 01:48:26,820
What do you mean?

803
01:48:46,880 --> 01:48:49,020
Emperor.

804
01:48:49,400 --> 01:48:51,960
The caravan coming from China to
Constantinie...

805
01:48:51,960 --> 01:48:53,960
...will pass Yenisehir.

806
01:48:55,740 --> 01:48:57,820
I will set up a great bazaar there.

807
01:48:59,420 --> 01:49:01,280
They will buy Turkmen's goods.

808
01:49:02,200 --> 01:49:05,760
But I will rule this bazaar.

809
01:49:08,820 --> 01:49:11,780
Turk goods are popular in my city.

810
01:49:13,680 --> 01:49:14,680
I accept.

811
01:49:16,140 --> 01:49:19,880
However, you will sell us cheaper.

812
01:49:20,500 --> 01:49:24,460
And the security of caravans is
your responsibility.

813
01:49:25,740 --> 01:49:28,240
Your job here is already hard.

814
01:49:28,240 --> 01:49:30,240
Don't worry.

815
01:49:30,240 --> 01:49:32,240
I will secure the caravans.

816
01:49:33,460 --> 01:49:35,580
We have made a strong ally, Osman Bey.

817
01:49:36,660 --> 01:49:38,640
But we have to find the enemy.

818
01:49:39,560 --> 01:49:40,640
Sen Tahor!

819
01:49:41,560 --> 01:49:42,640
He is a pawn.

820
01:49:43,440 --> 01:49:46,000
There is someone else behind him.
Who is that?

821
01:49:46,400 --> 01:49:48,120
We'll find out together.

822
01:49:49,260 --> 01:49:50,780
Whoever this is...

823
01:49:51,120 --> 01:49:53,120
...his dog Sen Tahor Revealed.

824
01:49:55,240 --> 01:49:57,540
Now he must find a new ally.

825
01:50:26,860 --> 01:50:29,300
Odin wanted our soul.

826
01:50:29,840 --> 01:50:30,840
We gave it.

827
01:50:31,840 --> 01:50:34,220
Now its our turn to take.

828
01:50:35,180 --> 01:50:36,220
Frig.

829
01:50:40,380 --> 01:50:44,040
You are a gift from tetchy oceans.

830
01:50:44,860 --> 01:50:47,120
The most beautiful among the Goddess'

831
01:51:01,200 --> 01:51:04,100
You happened to me from
the wrathful mountains...

832
01:51:04,700 --> 01:51:07,200
...my brutal tiger.

833
01:51:20,940 --> 01:51:22,160
Trudi!

834
01:51:32,360 --> 01:51:35,060
We are from the same mother!

835
01:51:38,640 --> 01:51:41,640
But I have three siblings now, not one!

836
01:51:58,300 --> 01:51:59,220
Saga!

837
01:51:59,640 --> 01:52:00,960
Where is Saga!

838
01:52:01,120 --> 01:52:03,920
He is coming soon!

839
01:52:12,280 --> 01:52:13,360
Let him come.

840
01:53:12,440 --> 01:53:14,300
I know why he is here.

841
01:53:47,820 --> 01:53:49,500
A gift for you.

842
01:53:55,100 --> 01:53:56,860
Easy!

843
01:54:01,080 --> 01:54:03,240
I am still the commander of this city!

844
01:54:03,240 --> 01:54:05,240
You must respect me!

845
01:54:05,300 --> 01:54:06,740
Do you hear me?!

846
01:54:06,840 --> 01:54:09,140
Respect me!

847
01:54:20,800 --> 01:54:21,980
Who are you?

848
01:54:34,740 --> 01:54:36,720
I asked who you are!

849
01:54:43,460 --> 01:54:45,100
I am your death.

850
01:55:47,260 --> 01:55:49,100
Glances of deads...

851
01:55:50,560 --> 01:55:52,440
...are beautiful.

852
01:56:15,550 --> 01:56:17,330
A gift from my Goddess to you.

853
01:56:19,520 --> 01:56:22,800
We saved your life, Kantakuzenos.

854
01:56:24,970 --> 01:56:27,320
We saved the new emperor of Rome.

855
01:56:36,970 --> 01:56:38,500
Sen Tahor.

856
01:56:40,100 --> 01:56:41,770
Whose dog were you?

857
01:56:46,840 --> 01:56:48,820
Damn it!
Who did it?!

858
01:56:50,100 --> 01:56:52,850
Sen Tahor's information was going to
reveal someone.

859
01:56:54,940 --> 01:56:57,910
I was going to have a target
if we were able to make him talk!

860
01:56:57,980 --> 01:56:59,750
Now I will burn the whole city!

861
01:57:01,960 --> 01:57:03,340
No, Emperor.

862
01:57:04,620 --> 01:57:05,850
Calm down.

863
01:57:07,180 --> 01:57:09,480
We will overcome this together.

864
01:57:09,840 --> 01:57:12,010
How, Osman Bey? How?

865
01:57:12,710 --> 01:57:14,700
I was about to lost my throne
at the show!

866
01:57:14,820 --> 01:57:16,590
And my captive dies in my dungeon!

867
01:57:17,580 --> 01:57:18,860
Who am I going to trust?

868
01:57:19,660 --> 01:57:22,890
You need to speak only to your
trusted people.

869
01:57:25,660 --> 01:57:27,550
We will be with you, Andranikos.

870
01:57:28,930 --> 01:57:30,750
We will not let those jackals
eat you.

871
01:57:32,730 --> 01:57:34,510
I appreciate this, Osman Bey.

872
01:57:35,330 --> 01:57:36,940
Always be careful.

873
01:57:38,160 --> 01:57:40,900
My Alps will be around the castle
just in case.

874
01:57:42,590 --> 01:57:43,710
Now...

875
01:57:45,730 --> 01:57:47,320
We got to go.

876
01:57:48,130 --> 01:57:49,350
May your path be clear.

877
01:57:50,100 --> 01:57:51,210
Eyvallah (thank you)

878
01:58:07,060 --> 01:58:08,250
Sen Tahor.

879
01:58:17,800 --> 01:58:20,560
Everything was private.
How did you find out?

880
01:58:21,030 --> 01:58:23,840
I also know that Turk Osman
ruined your game.

881
01:58:25,850 --> 01:58:26,880
How?

882
01:58:28,800 --> 01:58:30,960
The Gods of north whispered me.

883
01:58:43,440 --> 01:58:45,580
You did everything I wanted.

884
01:58:46,630 --> 01:58:47,770
What do you want?

885
01:59:00,890 --> 01:59:03,850
I don't let a lion die against many hyenas.

886
01:59:04,670 --> 01:59:07,200
And I won't let the cowards
take over the brave.

887
01:59:09,210 --> 01:59:10,710
Why do you do this?

888
01:59:11,240 --> 01:59:14,590
Because only the brave can eat
at Odin's table.

889
01:59:19,350 --> 01:59:20,670
What do you want from me?

890
01:59:28,670 --> 01:59:31,120
More than what you offered to Sen Tahor.

891
01:59:32,930 --> 01:59:34,050
An army.

892
01:59:41,160 --> 01:59:42,870
We will give you the throne.

893
01:59:44,780 --> 01:59:46,680
You will give us your army.

894
01:59:51,790 --> 01:59:52,910
Cheers.

895
01:59:55,410 --> 01:59:56,480
Cheers to what?

896
01:59:57,200 --> 01:59:58,480
To my unsuccess?

897
01:59:59,930 --> 02:00:01,390
To Osman's death.

898
02:00:31,360 --> 02:00:32,490
Brothers!

899
02:00:34,640 --> 02:00:37,260
All the masters who taught us to fight
have died!

900
02:00:37,680 --> 02:00:40,070
They are waiting for us
on the other side.

901
02:00:40,610 --> 02:00:43,530
Always remember who you are
and where you are coming from!

902
02:00:44,460 --> 02:00:46,220
Your armors cannot stop...

903
02:00:46,570 --> 02:00:48,750
...the wrath in your blood!

904
02:00:49,260 --> 02:00:51,110
Let your wrath come out and
kill them!

905
02:00:51,450 --> 02:00:52,760
Odin wants this!

906
02:00:53,050 --> 02:00:54,610
Olaf wants this!

907
02:00:54,780 --> 02:01:00,850
Death! Death! Death!

908
02:01:01,220 --> 02:01:02,200
Teger.

909
02:01:03,590 --> 02:01:04,680
They are coming.

910
02:01:06,150 --> 02:01:08,490
You are approaching your death, Osman.

911
02:01:09,900 --> 02:01:11,880
Brothers, let's go!

912
02:01:41,340 --> 02:01:42,600
Hello!

913
02:01:43,520 --> 02:01:45,120
Enjoy your new stall.

914
02:01:47,760 --> 02:01:48,800
Thank you.

915
02:01:50,800 --> 02:01:52,470
So you are Alcicek Hatun.

916
02:01:56,140 --> 02:01:57,330
Yes.

917
02:02:00,600 --> 02:02:01,610
Who are you?

918
02:02:01,930 --> 02:02:02,980
I am Ülgen.

919
02:02:03,360 --> 02:02:05,120
Osman Bey's mansion's cook.

920
02:02:10,760 --> 02:02:11,850
Hah, I know you.

921
02:02:11,950 --> 02:02:14,660
Praise be!
Those are beautiful.

922
02:02:17,390 --> 02:02:20,110
I wonder how your dowery looks like!

923
02:02:24,250 --> 02:02:27,620
Men won't let such a girl stay unmarried.

924
02:02:33,990 --> 02:02:37,080
There are no man to dare to marry me,
Ülgen sister.

925
02:02:39,200 --> 02:02:40,670
Masha Allah! (praise be)

926
02:02:41,120 --> 02:02:44,290
But you might be wrong.

927
02:02:45,620 --> 02:02:47,430
Tell me what kind of valiant you want.

928
02:02:47,660 --> 02:02:51,200
For example, I want a man who
eats the whole caldron.

929
02:02:54,190 --> 02:02:55,950
I haven't thought of it.

930
02:02:57,470 --> 02:02:59,110
But I am a picky one.

931
02:03:03,600 --> 02:03:06,070
First of all, he must fight
as well as I do.

932
02:03:07,420 --> 02:03:12,320
I want a valiant who would accompany
me in a war, not who would stop me.

933
02:03:12,770 --> 02:03:14,690
There is someone like this!

934
02:03:14,990 --> 02:03:16,100
You already know him!

935
02:03:16,320 --> 02:03:19,000
Inegol Martyr Gunduz Bey's son Aktemur!

936
02:03:30,850 --> 02:03:32,680
Aktemur?
The one I crushed?

937
02:03:34,550 --> 02:03:36,960
Mashallah.
You didn't forget him either.

938
02:03:41,760 --> 02:03:44,170
If you excuse me, I need to
see my mother now.

939
02:03:44,690 --> 02:03:45,770
Okay.

940
02:03:47,930 --> 02:03:49,410
This is done!

941
02:03:50,120 --> 02:03:53,600
Holy Creator, I will make those two marry
somehow.

942
02:03:54,190 --> 02:03:56,490
But I need help to marry as well.

943
02:03:57,190 --> 02:03:58,340
Amen.

944
02:04:10,110 --> 02:04:12,150
So Saga is after Osman.

945
02:04:13,240 --> 02:04:14,880
Sen Tahor is already dead.

946
02:04:16,370 --> 02:04:20,380
How did Osman manage to enter
the arena?

947
02:04:21,520 --> 02:04:23,200
How did he know everything?

948
02:04:24,030 --> 02:04:25,220
Sarkis.

949
02:04:25,920 --> 02:04:27,200
He is Osman's man.

950
02:04:28,230 --> 02:04:30,850
I will keep helping you.

951
02:04:41,390 --> 02:04:43,190
Alps! Ambush!

952
02:04:43,840 --> 02:04:45,460
Stay on alert!

953
02:05:27,390 --> 02:05:30,640
Osman!
Fight me like a real soldier!

954
02:05:31,550 --> 02:05:32,920
Fight so that you die early!

955
02:05:33,460 --> 02:05:35,360
We bothered the dogs.

956
02:05:36,000 --> 02:05:37,600
Of course they bark.

957
02:05:38,440 --> 02:05:40,000
Come to me.

958
02:05:42,630 --> 02:05:43,850
Alps!

959
02:05:44,790 --> 02:05:48,120
Don't show mercy until
we arrive in Yenisehir.

960
02:05:51,120 --> 02:05:52,930
Kill everyone you face!

961
02:05:53,390 --> 02:05:54,520
Attack!

962
02:05:57,990 --> 02:05:59,030
Allah is eternal!

963
02:05:59,080 --> 02:06:00,320
Allah is right!

964
02:07:14,740 --> 02:07:17,230
Your death will upset your friends!

965
02:07:17,230 --> 02:07:20,610
Do you see anyone upset around here?

966
02:07:25,840 --> 02:07:27,570
You will drown in your own blood!

967
02:07:27,600 --> 02:07:30,450
They told this to me before.
They are six feet under now.

968
02:07:30,450 --> 02:07:33,540
My place is not in the grave.
My place is in the table of Odin.

969
02:08:20,440 --> 02:08:22,100
Do you think I am hurt?

970
02:08:22,100 --> 02:08:25,170
You are not going to feel the pain
when I kill you.

971
02:09:09,760 --> 02:09:12,450
They will come for you, Osman.

972
02:09:14,520 --> 02:09:16,340
They will come for you.

973
02:09:16,370 --> 02:09:17,600
Let them come.

974
02:09:19,100 --> 02:09:20,450
Let them come.

975
02:09:22,080 --> 02:09:23,920
This land is a grave for the enemy...

976
02:09:24,110 --> 02:09:27,660
...and it's a homeland to our friends.

977
02:09:30,190 --> 02:09:32,780
I promise them the soil under this land.

978
02:10:25,660 --> 02:10:27,320
Alps.

979
02:10:29,140 --> 02:10:30,380
Prepare yourselves.

980
02:10:31,160 --> 02:10:32,550
We are going to Yenisehir.

981
02:10:32,580 --> 02:10:34,120
Eyvallah.

982
02:11:25,260 --> 02:11:27,360
They are coming!

983
02:11:32,960 --> 02:11:34,180
Saga.

984
02:11:41,060 --> 02:11:42,670
Saga! Saga!

985
02:11:43,100 --> 02:11:44,250
No!

986
02:11:50,220 --> 02:11:51,550
Brother.

987
02:11:54,890 --> 02:11:55,900
Brother.

988
02:11:56,530 --> 02:11:59,390
Saga, saga!

989
02:12:03,100 --> 02:12:05,470
No.
No!

990
02:12:08,450 --> 02:12:09,720
Saga!

991
02:12:12,020 --> 02:12:15,810
Osman killed Saga.

992
02:12:16,410 --> 02:12:17,840
Osman!

993
02:12:26,720 --> 02:12:28,800
Brother, brother!

994
02:12:47,810 --> 02:12:50,070
The flowing water will carry you away.

995
02:12:52,060 --> 02:12:54,480
You will be welcomed in the fairyland.

996
02:12:57,010 --> 02:12:58,960
Your place is Valhalla now.

997
02:13:01,040 --> 02:13:03,680
Your soul is a gift for Odin.

998
02:13:04,250 --> 02:13:06,100
Your blood is...

999
02:13:07,480 --> 02:13:09,060
...ours now.

1000
02:13:11,020 --> 02:13:12,850
Give Odin our best.

1001
02:13:16,820 --> 02:13:18,400
My little brother.

1002
02:13:26,560 --> 02:13:28,590
I swear on you!

1003
02:13:31,100 --> 02:13:35,590
If Odin doesn't help me avenge...

1004
02:13:36,940 --> 02:13:38,960
...I will walk with the devil!

1005
02:13:40,680 --> 02:13:42,310
Our blood shed!

1006
02:13:42,910 --> 02:13:45,840
I will not stop before killing many more!

1007
02:14:33,140 --> 02:14:35,030
The enemy is different.

1008
02:14:44,000 --> 02:14:46,060
Their weapon is different too.

1009
02:14:48,420 --> 02:14:49,840
They are new.

1010
02:14:51,500 --> 02:14:52,600
However...

1011
02:14:54,850 --> 02:14:57,250
I will erase them.

1012
02:15:06,490 --> 02:15:18,680
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com